/**
 * SocketManager handles all socket.io connection lifecycle,
 * event emission and reception on behalf of the API layer.
 *
 * Every lifecycle change and every event that crosses the wire is also written
 * to the client telemetry ring buffer (`./telemetry`) — that is what
 * API monitoring → "Socket events" renders. Only the event name, the payload
 * size and the timings are kept; payloads are never copied.
 *
 * ### Request / response over the socket
 *
 * Some server handlers are long running (file read, file diff): they run in a
 * worker pool and answer later with a dedicated *response event* carrying the
 * `request_id` of the request, so they can never answer the Socket.IO
 * acknowledgement. `request()` hides that protocol: it emits the request, keeps
 * the call pending and settles it when the matching response event arrives.
 *
 * @example
 * // codx-junior-file-read -> codx-junior-file-read-response
 * const { result } = await socket.request('codx-junior-file-read', {
 *   codx_path: '/path/to/project',
 *   path: 'src/main.js'
 * }, {
 *   responseEvent: 'codx-junior-file-read-response',
